A quantum feature map comprises of nonlinear encoding functions that are essential for generating an effective kernel estimate in the quantum space. The standard procedure for developing a quantum kernel estimate for classical input is to define a feature map that translates an input vector from classical feature \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
