The decision boundary visualizations thus help us present the argument that an appropriate interaction of quantum states through feature maps and appropriate hyperparameter tuning can lead to the formation of a suitable and complex decision boundary. In this study, input ranges and scaling are fixed to ensure robust feature map encoding and to maintain consistency with the formulation used in Suzuki et al.37. This setup leads the rotational factor \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
